# Lovable redesign gatekeeper

A whole-app redesign is in progress in Lovable. GitHub `main` on `AstroAii/purpledrw`
is the sync bus. Production does not auto-deploy on push during redesign.

## Baseline

Redesign starts from commit `7086ffa` on `main`. Full workflow:
`docs/LOVABLE-REDESIGN-WORKFLOW.md`. Preview env: `docs/LOVABLE-ENV-PARITY.md`.

## Agent duties

When Lovable may have pushed, or the user says "check Lovable":

1. `git fetch origin` and review `git log` / `git diff` against `origin/main`.
2. Run all quality gates: `check:em-dash`, `check:live-data`, `check:unique-images`,
   `check:lovable-auth`, `tsc --noEmit`, `build`, `check:entry-budget`.
3. Run Playwright smoke/responsive tests; prod e2e when creds available.
4. If migrations changed, verify schema against live DB before trusting UI.
5. Report Go/No-Go. On Go, ask the user before deploying live.
6. Before claiming done, sync documentation per `.cursor/rules/post-task-documentation.mdc` (handoff, `docs/`, rules, `AGENTS.md`, `mem/`).

## Hard rules

- Never deploy to `www.purplelife.org` without full gate pass and explicit user approval.
- Never assume Lovable UI is wired to real backend/schema without checking the diff.
- Fix backend/DB/routing issues in Cursor; give paste-ready Lovable prompts for pure UI fixes.
- CI runs on pushes to `main` and `lovable/redesign` plus all PRs; deploy workflow is manual only (`workflow_dispatch`).

## Lovable pitfalls to catch

- Missing `<Outlet/>` on parent routes with children
- Queries to non-existent tables/columns
- New tables without RLS
- Hardcoded colors instead of theme tokens
- Em dashes, placeholder marketing data, duplicate hero images
- Wrong Supabase ref (must be `xxnzmfzsjplrutrgbzxy` via env, not hardcoded)
